---
import Video from '../components/Video.astro'
import { modules } from '../data/curriculum'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { isLivePath } from '../lib/content'
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The Full Curriculum to become a professional Full-Stack Developer"
  description="Get the complete roadmap (from start to finish) on how to become a job-ready, competent JavaScript developer."
>
  <div class="container-md">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>The Complete Full-Stack Development Curriculum</h1>
      <p class="lead">Go from zero to a professional Full-Stack developer.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="callout intro">
      <strong>Important:</strong> This curriculum gives you complete training on the deep technical concepts, homework,
      cheat sheets, and practice projects, so you become a highly-skilled software developer.{' '}
      <strong>Watch the video to get a proper walkthrough.</strong>
    </div>

    <figure class="intro-video">
      <Video source="q87DYpgqfhE" title="How to get the most out of The Full Curriculum" />
      <figcaption>How to get the most out of The Full Curriculum</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="copy">
      <p>
        By the time you are done with this curriculum you will have the complete skills to code and launch modern websites,
        web applications and even mobile apps from scratch. Plus you will have an impressive portfolio to land you a
        respectable job as a software developer.
      </p>
      <p>
        We’ll do all of this while focusing on one programming language, which is JavaScript. JavaScript is currently the
        most popular and versatile programming language on planet internet. In fact, 99% (maybe even 100%) of all top
        websites use JavaScript, and all the tech giants use it to build their websites and mobile apps such as Facebook,
        PayPal, Google, LinkedIn, Walmart, Tesla, Apple, and even Microsoft uses it actively to build their apps.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Trust the process — follow the modules.</strong> Each module has core training along with a ton of practice
        projects. These practice projects will give you real-life training on how to think like a developer and go from a
        blank screen to a fully finished application.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card total">
      <p class="eyebrow">Time to completion</p>
      <p class="total-value">5 months</p>
      <p class="muted">Study 15 hrs/week and complete within 5 months.</p>
    </div>

    {modules.map(mod => (
      <section class="module">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">{mod.eyebrow}</p>
          <h2>{mod.title}</h2>
          <p class="lead">{mod.description}</p>
          {mod.time && <p class="time"><strong>{mod.time.label}:</strong> {mod.time.value}</p>}
          {mod.note && <p class="callout"><strong>Note:</strong> {mod.note}</p>}
        </header>

        {mod.groups.map(group => (
          <div class="group">
            <h3>{group.title}</h3>
            <ul class="training">
              {group.items.map(item => {
                const live = isLivePath(item.link)
                const Tag = live ? 'a' : 'div'
                return (
                  <li>
                    <Tag href={live ? item.link : undefined} class:list={['training-item', { unavailable: !live }]}>
                      <img src={item.thumbSrc} alt="" loading="lazy" />
                      <span class="name">{item.name}</span>
                      {!live && <span class="badge">Not currently available</span>}
                    </Tag>
                  </li>
                )
              })}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}

        {mod.outcomes && (
          <div class="group">
            <h3>Module outcomes</h3>
            <p>Once you are done with this module you will be able to:</p>
            <ol>{mod.outcomes.map(o => <li>{o}</li>)}</ol>
          </div>
        )}
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .intro-video { margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .intro-video figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 8px; }
  .copy p { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .total { text-align: center; margin-block: 32px 48px; }
  .total-value { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; }
  .total .muted { margin: 0; }

  .module {
    padding-block: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .module:last-child { margin-bottom: var(--section); }
  .module h2 { margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
  .time { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
  .group { margin-top: 32px; }
  .group h3 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .training {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 200px), 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .training-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    height: 100%;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .training-item img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }
  a.training-item:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  a.training-item:hover img { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .unavailable { color: var(--muted); }
  .unavailable img { filter: grayscale(1); opacity: 0.55; }
  .unavailable .badge { align-self: flex-start; }
</style>
